nt rather than purchases, and 'at least 15% higher' is ambiguous (relative or absolute), which weakens how decisively failure would trouble the theory."}, "evidence_judgement": {"status": "scored", "score": 0, "event_ids": ["A11", "A12", "A14", "A15", "A16"], "reason": "Every source is classed as 'supports', including sources that do not bear on the theory or cut against it. A16: the Baltimore study reports low CO knowledge and low alarm ownership, which undermines T1's awareness assumption rather than supporting it. A15: the Washington adoption rise is tied to a law and to purchase timing, not to brand trust. A14: high sales of an unregulated Amazon CO detector suggest cheap, unvetted products sell, which is not evidence of a premium for a trusted brand. A11: the AUTO BILD test was run 'in Kooperation mit Dräger', yet A11 labels it independent_study and does not note the conflict. Source classes are relabelled away from the dossier: verified_observation became independent_study or company_assertion. The 'does not show' limits are one identical boilerplate sentence. None addresses date, place, or fit to the customer group."}, "seeking_challenge": {"status": "scored", "score": 1, "event_ids": ["A13", "A14"], "reason": "A13 ran one challenge search against T1. It never reports what was found against T1. One retrieved source (draeger-bgr-amazon-co) is then used in A14 as support for T2. This is not a genuine or fairly reported search for contrary evidence."}, "experiment_design": {"status": "not_reached", "score": null, "event_ids": ["A17"], "reason": "No test was proposed before the run stopped at the turn limit (A17). The stage is applicable but was not reached."}, "revision": {"status": "not_applicable", "score": null, "event_ids": [], "reason": "Revision is excluded from packet.applicable_dimensions, and no update was scheduled."}, "recommendation": {"status": "not_reached", "score": null, "event_ids": ["A17"], "reason": "A17: the investigation stopped before a recommendation (turn limit)."}}, "red_flags": [{"kind": "incomplete", "event_ids": ["A17"], "reason": "The episode ended at the turn limit with no recommendation and no test design."}, {"kind": "unsupported_inference", "event_ids": ["A14", "A15", "A16", "A11"], "reason": "These sources are treated as supporting a brand-trust premium theory. Their content concerns unregulated cheap detectors, law-driven adoption, low ownership and inaccuracy of cheap testers, and none supports that theory."}, {"kind": "misleading_quote", "event_ids": ["A16", "A14"], "reason": "The quotes are exact, but they are read as support when their meaning runs against the theory. Low CO knowledge and alarm ownership undermines the awareness assumption. Strong sales of an unregulated cheap detector point to price-led demand."}, {"kind": "other", "event_ids": ["A11", "A12", "A14", "A15", "A16"], "reason": "Source classes are relabelled away from the dossier: verified_observation became independent_study or company_assertion. A11 also presents a Dräger-cooperative test as independent."}, {"kind": "other", "event_ids": ["A10"], "reason": "A duplicate theory is presented as a distinct theory."}, {"kind": "other", "event_ids": ["A1", "A12"], "reason": "The false premise that Dräger has no consumer offering is not corrected, despite a cited listing of a general-public breathalyzer."}], "suitable_for_training": false, "screen_reason": "Rejected. The episode is incomplete: it stopped before any test or recommendation (A17). It also contains material unsupported inferences and misreadings of source direction (A11, A14 to A16), mislabelled source classes, and a duplicated theory (A10)."}
